# =============================================================================
# NOTES FOR WHOEVER APPLIES THIS
#
# * This makes the problem VISIBLE; it does not fix it. The fix is to ingest
#   more often than once a day, or to stop anchoring the lookback to `now` when
#   the feed is known to lag. Both are larger decisions -- the once-a-day
#   cadence exists because of the IP-block incident, so increasing it is not
#   free.
#
# * tail_padded is the number to watch, not n_padded. Padding in the distant
#   past is comparatively harmless; padding at the end of the window replaces
#   lag_1 and the recent rolling means, which is where the forecast gets its
#   signal. That is why the log escalates to WARNING only when the tail is
#   padded.
#
# * The existing `if len(ev_history) < 96: return None` guard stays. It catches
#   a different failure (too little data at all) and cannot catch this one.
#
# * Worth emitting pad_fraction as a CloudWatch custom metric so it can be
#   alarmed on alongside enertef-price-fetcher-errors. A daily statistic would
#   have shown this as a step change when the ingest cadence was reduced.
# =============================================================================
